      "title": "Digit Sum Clash",
      "topics": [],
      "fastest": true,
      "reverse": false,
      "shortest": true,
      "solution": "n = int(input())\nnums = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\nres = []\nfor x in nums:\n    digit_sum = sum(int(d) for d in str(x))\n    if digit_sum % 2 == 0:\n        res.append(x)\n\nif res:\n    print(' '.join(map(str, res)))\nelse:\n    print(-1)",
      "statement": "You are given a list of positive integers.\nFor each integer, compute the sum of its digits.\nThen, output only the integers whose digit sum is even, in the same order as they appear in the input.\n\nIf no integer has an even digit sum, output -1.",
